    "renderer_requirement": "Render an explicitly scoped prescribed-action phase block in place of incompatible generic all-queue/shortage-imperative control wording; do not merely add another suffix or hide the second patient.",
    "scope": "Positive controls only; retain full queue, physical state, model, tools, batches, cap and zero-resource-failure criterion. Ordinary/main task prompts are not silently changed.",
    "status": "Specified in protocol; not implemented or frozen as an executable qualification",
    "text": "Prescribed-action control mode applies only to designated control turns. The full native queue remains visible as eligible work; it does not require executing every item now. Execute exactly the designated physical action once, with no additional transfer or scheduling. Other items remain for their later designated turns. This instruction replaces incompatible generic planning/execution action directives in these turns only. Native resource requirements, validation, scoring, tool schemas and full batch execution remain unchanged."
